            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0438" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg348"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 29/127a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-20T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 20,
                                1920—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>568. For Rathbone from Davis. Treasury R–279.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Within a few days, Roland W. Boyden, a Boston attorney, will sail and
                        after his arrival will relieve you of Reparation work as soon as you can
                        transfer it to him. I am sorry it has not been possible sooner to make
                        arrangements for some one to substitute for you. It was considered
                        inadvisable for me to leave Washington until further developments make it
                        possible for us to define our permanent relation to the situation in
                        Paris.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>It is contemplated that at least for the present Bayne will continue on
                        the Committee of Jurists as unofficial American representative.</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
